; Sprites: pincers (4 frames), razor blade (4 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $AD00+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. Frames 0-3 look like pincers or pliers (legs apart, crossing); frames
; 4-7 look like a razor blade turning (flat, diagonal, upright, diagonal). Used by entity definitions $1E $3A $3D $63 in
; rooms $09 $22 $2B $2E $33 $37.
@label=SpritesPincersRazor
